CSS overflow controls how content is handled when it doesn’t fit inside an element’s box. It helps manage scrolling and visibility of extra content.Can hide, scroll, or show overflowing content.      Common values include visible, hidden, scroll, and auto.  Useful for keeping layouts neat and preventing content overlap.
